WEBVTT

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:44.220
At 18:00 Space Standard Time,

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.940
a GDF Special Forces unit
set up transmission satellites

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:51.670
to replace the ones destroyed by the
United Pan-Galactic Empire,

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:53.780
also known as Wulgaru.

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:56.740
However, the unit was
rushed by a Wulgaru squad.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.530
Although they tried to counter the attack,
they were nonetheless overpowered

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:02.580
and the replacement transmission
satellites were destroyed.

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:07.710
Consequentially, we are currently unable
to send transmissions to Undina.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.220
Several years have passed
since the invading

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:12.760
"Surprise Attack"

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:14.160
Wulgaru army suddenly appeared in our solar system,

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.880
but we still do not know the

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:18.810
motive behind their invasion
and acts of destruction.

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:21.800
The news keeps going on about us.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.750
So Wulgaru are actually called
the Half Fried Rice Tofu Empire...

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:27.960
That wasn't even close...

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.670
Are you too stupid to
even have common sense?

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.860
I can go through life
without common sense!

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.590
What type of retort was that?

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.130
They keep showing the
clip where I botched it.

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:40.220
Check out my Asagi Special.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.600
Knock it off! Not before my checkup.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:54.670
Man, even our cutting-edge
units look pathetic...

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:56.920
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.450
Nah, you didn't make us wait any!

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.930
I'd like the boys to proceed to
Examination Room 1

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:08.620
and the girls to proceed to the
Measurements Room.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:09.910
Okay!

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.800
I've gained! I knew I gained weight!

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.130
Let's try that again...

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:23.970
It will turn out the same each time.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:27.350
It just says I've gained because of
the sudden bursts of gravity!

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.860
I don't wanna drink that...

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:41.900
You can choose from a
selection of flavors.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.390
It comes in yogurt,
vanilla and chocolate.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.200
I'll let you decide!

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:59.440
Sheesh! That crazy stunt is
giving us a run for our money.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:02.410
Could you make the five
units activate quicker?

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:03.460
Forget it!

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:06.000
Just getting them all operational
is near-enough miraculous.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.620
That isn't good enough!

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.590
I can't do what I can't do.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:13.920
And could you make the linkage
a simpler auto function?

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:14.770
I'll think about it.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:19.090
None of them have mastered
the JURIA-SYSTEM yet,

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:22.810
so it's our job to help
them however we can.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:26.640
Please take your job more seriously,
Head Mechanic.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:30.490
There is a difference between
"serious" and "frantic," Rin-Rin.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:34.870
You've gotta relax some.
Otherwise you're going to break.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:42.150
A Special Forces unit set up
new transmission satellites.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.300
When rushed by a Wulgaru squad,
they tried to counter the attack.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:46.840
However, they were-

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:46.840
Not again!

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:50.270
You've got it lucky!

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:54.080
They only show the part
where you managed to fire a shot.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:55.920
Just like a hero to steal the glory.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:57.200
Thank you!

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.250
That wasn't a compliment!

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.300
Huh? But you just said...

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:04.490
You're all done.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.970
Detailed reports will
be ready in a few days,

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:10.530
but from what I saw today,
everyone seems to be doing fine.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.440
Thank you very much.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:13.960
Isn't that great news?

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:14.710
Totally!

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:16.530
Have you finished your exams?

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:17.610
Uh, yes.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.880
Then move over to the briefing room.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:20.790
Huh?

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:22.840
We will explain your next mission there.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:27.200
Everyone, get running!

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.200
How are they?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.570
From what I saw, I'm worried about
psychological fatigue.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:41.020
I believe they could use some down time
instead of another mission.

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:46.160
Aren't those children more developed
than normal humans in some areas?

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.250
Toshikazu Asagi is able to process
vast amounts of data.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:52.350
Kei Kugimiya has highly developed
auditory perception.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.620
Tamaki Irie has an abnormally
high G-tolerance.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:58.190
Ataru Suruga has outstanding
memory in select areas.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.960
Izuru Hitachi has an excellent
capacity to concentrate.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:04.230
But it looks like these strengths
are hard on their bodies.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.180
Why did you choose those five?

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:10.200
I'm sure there were more
evenly balanced students.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:14.610
All five of them showed
top-class survival instincts.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:16.140
That made them ideal
pilots for AHSMB units,

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:18.570
which were installed with the JURIA-SYSTEM.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:20.310
I see...

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:23.170
Also, about Izuru Hitachi...

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:25.670
He may require a reexamination.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:26.590
Why is that?

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:29.990
I cannot pinpoint the problem,
hence the reexamination.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:32.410
I see.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:37.140
Jeez, what are they going
to make us do next?

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:39.420
This is depressing.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.020
At ease.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:45.090
Sir.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:48.260
GDF Headquarters is calling you to arms.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:51.150
They found an enemy supply route.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:55.180
Your next mission will be to launch
a surprise attack on their supply ships.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.120
We're attacking them?

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.120
That is why it's called
a surprise attack!

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:02.500
The mission commences in
36 hours. That is all.

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:06.230
Sir, could you go over
the mission in more detail...?

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:07.920
I will right before you set out.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:10.950
Uh, were we the ones
assigned to this mission?

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:12.660
That was a pointless question.

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.390
Yesterday's mission ended in failure

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:17.830
and we still aren't accustomed
to piloting the AHSMBs.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.250
Your opinion has been dismissed.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:23.710
They'll brutalize me if I fail again...

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.580
I thought we'd finally become heroes,
but we're still losers...

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.340
Will we be the Failure Five forever?

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:33.090
Team Rabbits!

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:35.740
You have been authorized
to take a day and a half off.

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:38.000
The ship is ready for takeoff
as soon as you are ready.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:38.770
Time off?

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:39.990
Right!

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.810
You get to go on a vacation,
albeit a short one.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:43.670
Meet Your Special Someone in this
Charming and Relaxing Vacation Spot
PARADISE RESORT

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:44.540
Awesome!

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.570
Isn't this is a super expensive resort?

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:51.990
Resort! Vacation! Romance!

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:53.990
Time off before a mission?

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:56.740
So we won't die with any regrets?

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:58.990
Guys, you should be happy about this!

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:01.670
Resort. Vacation! ROMANCE!

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:03.500
Enough with that lame cheer.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:05.940
We're only getting a day and a half off.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:08.130
After that, we have to hit the enemy
with a sneak attack.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:09.250
Even so...!

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:12.450
Resort! Vacation! Romance! Yay!

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:31.490
Whoo boy! Look at all the babes!

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:34.140
And all the dudes!

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:42.770
<i>...unit set transmission satellites to replace
the ones destroyed by the Wulgaru.</i>

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:44.310
<i>However, the unit was
rushed by a Wulgaru squad</i>

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:47.290
<i>and the replacement transmission
satellites were destroyed.</i>

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:50.900
Uh, aren't you getting hungry?
Why don't we grab a bite to eat?

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:52.950
I don't want your commiseration!

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:56.060
They're open all hours of the day, huh?

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:59.010
Just what I'd expect from a resort!

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:01.140
No matter what we eat,
the army's footing the bill, right?

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:03.100
I'm getting curry!

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.960
A big bowl of rice
with salted fish guts!

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:05.640
They won't have that.

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:07.880
Those are the kids they're
showing on the news.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.570
Yeah. I'm just like, "Are
they gifted or not?"

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:10.960
What are they doing here?

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.480
Did they finish a mission?

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:15.340
It's not like this is
anything new, y'know?

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:17.510
When you get down to it,
we're the Failure Five.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:20.560
We may have high specs, but we're still
failures for some odd reason.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.490
We heard that crap all the time
at school, remember?

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:24.650
Everyone at school saying that

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:27.100
isn't the same as the whole galaxy saying it!

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.240
I'm going to the cottage.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:36.090
Same.

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:38.660
Damn, they're such party poops!

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:40.220
They should enjoy the resort since we're here!

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:41.720
Seriously.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.020
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:45.480
Here is your white rice
and pickled fish guts.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.610
Who ordered the curry?

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:52.630
Man, the party's starting to heat up!

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:54.030
I'm totally getting pumped!

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:55.600
I'm going.

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:58.290
Wait! If you're gonna hit the town...

00:09:58.290 --> 00:09:59.900
No, I'm going to train.

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:00.910
Train?

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:04.540
After a hero fails, 80% of the time
he goes on a training spree!

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:47.660
Welcome back.

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:49.270
Where's Asagi?

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:50.280
Sleeping.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:52.980
Where are Suruga and Tamaki?

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.030
They said that they were going
to enjoy their vacation.

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.070
Kei?

00:10:58.070 --> 00:10:58.760
Yes?

00:10:59.740 --> 00:11:01.550
You've got some cream here...

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:07.810
Cake!

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:11.810
It'll be ready soon. Want some?

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:19.740
Well?

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:22.660
It's sweet, I guess...

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:26.030
It wouldn't be a cake
if it wasn't sweet.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:27.930
It's super sweet.

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:29.640
Got a problem with my recipe?!

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:30.790
Uh, no!

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:37.000
I wonder what we're doing
in a place like this.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.000
Until just recently, we were students.

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:44.130
I figured we'd be put on
the battlefield eventually,

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:46.270
but this was so sudden...

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:48.750
They keep sending us
on one mission after the next.

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:50.720
They even ordered us to take leave...

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:56.470
But we can't choose anything else
for ourselves, can we?

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:00.230
We were born to fight.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:03.580
All of our memories were erased
before we entered the academy...

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:06.950
If they order us to go, we have
no choice but to fight.

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:09.950
Sometimes it's too much to bear.

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:11.910
Just what am I?

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:14.510
I can't even make decisions for myself.

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:18.300
Izuru, doesn't it bother you?

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:20.690
It doesn't matter.

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:22.260
Even if I don't have a past,

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:24.620
even if my future is nasty,
it doesn't matter to a hero.

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:25.470
What?

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:27.820
When I first entered the academy,

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:29.780
I spent all of my time reading
the manga in the dorm.

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:33.000
Those manga were brimming
with cool heroes.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.480
I thought it would be awesome
if I could be like them.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:37.320
I think that if we can
accomplish something,

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:40.890
it will prove that we were born for a reason
precisely because we started with nothing.

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:46.650
We may be the Failure Five,
but let's work to become heroes together!

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:51.250
Heroes, huh?

00:12:53.690 --> 00:12:56.190
Would you like another slice of cake?

00:12:56.190 --> 00:12:57.720
Gimme just a sec!

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:04.230
Could you tell me what you think?

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.220
I just know you'll appreci-

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:08.180
No!

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:10.950
Ladies, you've got such nice bodies!

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:11.700
If I compared you to guns,

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:13.480
I'd say you're as wonderful as the

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:16.000
Beretta Cx4 Storm designed
by Master Giugiaro.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:19.380
It has an elegant bodyline with curves
reminiscent of a violin!

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:20.650
At any rate, practicality has nothing to do
with the pursuit of a beautiful body!

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:23.400
At any rate, practicality has nothing to do
with the pursuit of a beautiful body!

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:24.270
Why'd we all come to the pool?

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:26.360
Of course, guns overflowing with
beautiful functionality rock!

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:26.190
Because this is a resort?

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:28.540
But your dazzlingly beautiful bodylines
make you like

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:27.390
Say...

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:28.470
Hell no.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:31.620
thoroughbreds amongst pack horses,
diamonds amongst glass beads

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:33.960
and silver chips amongst lead balls!

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:42.920
At last! Resort! Vacation! Romance!

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:09.720
He has a girlfriend...

00:14:10.550 --> 00:14:11.910
She must be his sister!

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:18.670
Who are you?!

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:20.080
Hey!

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:33.720
Let us be off.

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:36.870
But I still haven't told him how I feel!

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:40.570
Hey, can he swim?

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:44.570
Don't invite us to the friggin' pool
if you can't swim.

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:46.550
I-I'm sorry.

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:49.800
Hey, so, do you know that girl?
Who was she?

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:50.720
No, I don't...

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:54.580
And you tried to ask her out?
I could never do that!

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:55.740
You did not say that.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:58.250
But... I've seen her somewhere...

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:01.530
How was your vacation?

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:08.820
Go get changed and meet
back here in one hour.

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:11.300
A man from GDF Headquarters will be
supervising this mission;

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:13.390
you will meet him then.

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:18.680
This is GDF's Vice Chief
of Staff, Captain Komine.

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:22.330
Attention!

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:25.550
At ease.

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:30.180
The Vice Chief of Staff will personally
command this upcoming mission.

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:33.120
That is an indication of just how
important this operation is.

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:37.040
Thus far, the GDF has
only fought in defense.

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:40.110
But with the completion
of these new AHSMB

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:42.810
units and you as their highly-trained pilots,

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:47.050
we are finally able to take an aggressive
stance and initiate an attack.

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:52.030
This mission is crucial for stopping
the Wulgaru invasion. Therefore-

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:54.280
Sir, I apologize for
interrupting your speech,

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:56.850
but could you please introduce me?

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:00.700
This is my adjutant, Lt. Amane.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:03.480
Explain the upcoming mission.

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:09.350
We discovered a set Wulgaru
route from beta 25 to 27

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:11.740
on Jupiter's third
quadrant orbital grid.

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:16.640
We believe there is a high probability
that it is a supply route.

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:18.540
This is where we will strike!

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:22.180
It is currently amidst a particularly
strong solar storm.

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:26.230
Soon the area will be bathed
in extremely powerful CME

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:25.770
Note: CME is the acronym
for "Coronal Mass Ejection"

00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:28.540
and high-energy charged particles.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.720
As a result, many electronics,

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:34.370
including radar, should be
rendered temporarily inoperable.

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:35.930
Wait for the enemy to go blind

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:37.430
and then crush them when
they fall into disarray!

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:41.590
You will wait for the solar flare
to pass behind a planetoid

00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:43.600
that has a powerful shield in place.

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:45.470
It will take 24 seconds at full speed

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:48.270
to reach the enemy's anticipated location
from behind the shielded planetoid.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:50.760
We expect the enemy's systems
to recover in 40 seconds.

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:54.300
You have 16 seconds to destroy
everything and pull back.

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:57.280
This operation requires
clockwork precision.

00:16:57.280 --> 00:17:01.500
As such, I shall be issuing
the orders from start to finish.

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:04.360
You are still inexperienced soldiers
fresh from the academy.

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:08.010
You may possess latent abilities,
but you are painfully lacking in experience.

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:11.510
You must not perform pathetically
like in your prior operation.

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:13.170
Have I made myself clear?

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:15.090
We have dedicated a large portion

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:17.550
of our budget to you, not
just the AHSMB units!

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:22.140
If you fail to perform accordingly,
it defeats the point in ever creating you!

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:25.840
Sir, it is about time they
prepared for takeoff.

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:29.710
The AHSMBs' maintenance is complete.
You may see them if you like.

00:17:29.710 --> 00:17:31.340
I could show you the way.

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:36.450
You are to go to your cockpits.

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:39.780
How dare he say,
"It defeats the point in creating you"?!

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:42.460
It's not like he's our
creator or anything!

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:45.660
Grr! He totally pissed me off!

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:48.170
"Perform pathetically
like last time," huh?

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:50.820
That's what got you upset?

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:53.570
Well, this time we're
going after supply ships.

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:56.820
And we should have the upper hand
since it's a surprise attack.

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:58.750
I don't want you to trying
to make me feel better!

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:02.310
In any event, we have
to fight under some

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:05.360
old fart who resembles
a squashed cream puff.

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:07.060
Yep! Let's do our best!

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:11.650
That's not how most people
would typically respond.

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:13.380
Pay attention to the conversation.

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:15.380
Stupy-dupy poopy.

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:17.850
Quit randomly trying to console people.

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:25.830
Gordinion is ready for takeoff.

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:27.470
Roger.

00:18:27.470 --> 00:18:29.690
Commander Simon, what will you be doing?

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:31.000
I will remain on standby here.

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:35.650
Understood. That would make things
less strenuous on me as well.

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:37.930
I will be careful with how I inform
the Vice Chief of Staff.

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:39.840
Where is Simon?

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:42.640
He is on standby at Headquarters.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:46.660
Well, it was merely his
job to nurse the MJP.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:49.330
It is our job to properly utilize them.

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:50.770
Takeoff in T minus 30 seconds.

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:08.290
Heavy armor?

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:11.710
Are we getting fully outfitted 'cause
the Vice Chief of Staff is in command?

00:19:12.350 --> 00:19:14.170
The grill ads are gone!

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:17.610
Probably because this
isn't getting aired.

00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:19.740
That or we've lost our sponsors.

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:20.430
Already?

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:23.930
May I not goof up this time!
May I not goof up this time!

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:26.290
I've confirmed that the Pits are
in position for blast off.

00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:27.850
All vessels are prepared for blast off.

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:29.510
All ships: Blast off!

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:31.650
Thank you.

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:34.270
I hear they went to a resort.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:36.710
When do you think we'll get to go?

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:39.320
Wulgaru ships spotted at Point D7.

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:47.240
All units, get into battle formation!

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:51.810
I'm putting them on the screen.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:57.470
A supply fleet? Really?

00:19:58.460 --> 00:19:59.470
What are those?

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:01.660
They don't appear to be supply ships.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:03.120
Then what are they?

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:05.120
I believe this is an armed
reconnaissance squadron.

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:06.950
Wasn't this a supply route?!

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:08.440
That was merely speculation.

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:10.610
You are the one who determined
it to be a supply route.

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:12.730
We should avoid contact.

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:15.590
Are you saying to pull back
without achieving anything?!

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:18.800
Doesn't the JURIA-SYSTEM demonstrate
its prowess best in situations like this?!

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:20.520
Commence Operation Night Blow!

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:22.840
Commence the operation!

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:24.620
Mission: Start!

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:27.510
I had the units fully
outfitted just to be safe

00:20:27.510 --> 00:20:29.990
as we were unsure what type of
enemy vessels they may encounter.

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:30.830
That's a given!

00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:34.540
Attack!

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:36.130
Orders to attack?

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:37.580
My AHSMB is terrified!

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:39.050
You mean you are!

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:40.760
No!

00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:44.550
Don't run from a fight! Attack!

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:50.390
I'll cover you!

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:57.980
They're quick!

00:20:58.330 --> 00:21:00.280
They're fast! This squadron
is using cutting-edge units!

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:02.190
Incoming attack from the front right!

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:05.450
They're quick to dodge.

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:06.620
Here's the next attack!

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:10.700
And they're good at defense.

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:12.370
They can't win! Issue a retreat.

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:13.540
I can't do that!

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:15.850
We are clearly at a disadvantage!

00:21:15.850 --> 00:21:17.980
If you're going to state your opinion,
give information to back it!

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:19.130
How are they at a disadvantage?!

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:21.130
Can't you see that for yourself?

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:27.780
I can't hit 'em!

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:36.350
How are we supposed to fight them?!

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:38.810
Rose 3!

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:40.210
S-sir!

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:41.870
What are you doing?! Charge!

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:44.860
Didn't you hear me?
Charge at full speed!

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:46.360
Uh, okay!

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:47.450
Wait, Tamaki!

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:48.950
Rose 3, activate shields!

00:21:50.140 --> 00:21:50.890
Tamaki?!

00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:00.750
My shields...!

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:07.890
Tamaki!

00:23:40.870 --> 00:23:55.890
"Loss"
